> Tests for Example Benefit Eligibility Rules

```catala
declaration scope TestBenefitEligibility:
  benefit_eligibility scope BenefitEligibility
```

### Test 1: Eligible individual with low income

```catala
scope TestBenefitEligibility:
  definition benefit_eligibility.individual equals Individual {
    -- age: 30
    -- income: $12,000
    -- is_resident: true
  }
  assertion benefit_eligibility.result.eligible
  assertion benefit_eligibility.result.monthly_amount = $500
```

### Test 2: Ineligible individual (underage)

```catala
declaration scope TestBenefitIneligibleAge:
  benefit_eligibility scope BenefitEligibility

scope TestBenefitIneligibleAge:
  definition benefit_eligibility.individual equals Individual {
    -- age: 16
    -- income: $10,000
    -- is_resident: true
  }
  assertion benefit_eligibility.result.eligible = false
```

### Test 3: Ineligible individual (income too high)

```catala
declaration scope TestBenefitIneligibleIncome:
  benefit_eligibility scope BenefitEligibility

scope TestBenefitIneligibleIncome:
  definition benefit_eligibility.individual equals Individual {
    -- age: 25
    -- income: $35,000
    -- is_resident: true
  }
  assertion benefit_eligibility.result.eligible = false
```

### Test 4: Mid-tier benefit amount

```catala
declaration scope TestBenefitMidTier:
  benefit_eligibility scope BenefitEligibility

scope TestBenefitMidTier:
  definition benefit_eligibility.individual equals Individual {
    -- age: 40
    -- income: $20,000
    -- is_resident: true
  }
  assertion benefit_eligibility.result.eligible
  assertion benefit_eligibility.result.monthly_amount = $300
```
